#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""apps-evidence — the owner-proof page (readable edition).

Reads /Users/nakfaai/.dsh/state/apps-status.json (what the stores actually say),
/Users/nakfaai/.dsh/state/apps-pending.json (what waits on Ammaniel's yes) and
every app's evidence folder /Users/nakfaai/output/apps/evidence/<slug>/ (what
its own Bot proved), then writes /Users/nakfaai/output/apps/evidence.html.

The page leads with the verdict and the pictures. The Bot's long report is
rendered as real markdown behind one fold, so the proof stays one click deep
instead of a wall of raw pipes and hashes. Nothing here is typed by hand: a
fact shows only if it is in the JSON, in a STATUS.md, or in a file under the
app's evidence folder.

  apps-evidence            read + write the page
  apps-evidence page       re-render only (same thing)
"""
